    "body": "Closes #40458\n\n## Problem\n\ndir.lua cannot be re-used by anything else. plugins like archive.lua mentioned in #32280 would greatly benefit from this.\n\n## Solution\n\nRefactors the built-in directory browser into a conservative, internal listing UI. Dogfood this shape through the existing filesystem lister as a POC.\n\nNew terminology:\n- provider (`nvim.dir.Provider`): a consumer/source adapter of the directory viewer api, providing the below methods\n- ctx (`nvim.dir.Ctx`): metadata around a provider-managed buffer\n\n| Surface | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `nvim.dir.open(buf, name, provider)` | Open `buf` as a listing named `name` using a provider. |\n| `Provider.list_entries(ctx, cb)` | produce entries or error |\n| `Provider.open_entry(ctx, entry)` | open/refresh the entry under the cursor |\n| `Provider.open_parent(ctx)` | handle parent navigation |\n| `Provider.attach(ctx)` | run source-specific buffer setup after initial render |\n\nEnsure that `-` stays globally mapped to the filesystem provider.\n\n",
    "closed_at": null,
